  "description": "In response to the climate emergency, Camden Council’s Local Plan includes Policy CC5, which aims to improve the sustainability of existing buildings through enhanced insulation, upgraded windows and doors, and low-carbon heating systems like heat pumps. Primrose Hill Primary School has been identified as a priority due to its poor energy performance, driven by large rooms, high ceilings, and single-glazed windows.\nTo address this, the proposal includes installing ground source heat pumps and improving the building fabric to reduce energy demand. These upgrades align with Policy CC6, promoting long-term energy efficiency.\nKey measures include:\nSecondary Glazing: Installation throughout the main building using Historic England-approved styles to preserve the building’s heritage.\nInternal Wall Insulation (IWI): Applied to about 50% of external walls, avoiding areas with historic features. Cornices and picture rails will be replicated, and the IWI will be fully reversible.\nGround Source Heat Pumps:  Installation of Ground Source Heat Pump ,with 40–45 boreholes drilled in the playground, which will be restored post-installation. \nPassive Cooling: The heat pump system will also provide cooling via fan convectors, using ground-cooled water to maintain comfortable indoor temperatures without refrigerants to a number of rooms that exhibit overheating for a number of months throughout the year.",
